@page "/privacy"
@page "/privacy-policy"
@layout SPIC.MauiBlazorApp.Shared.Layout.EmptyLayout
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - SPIC ONE</PageTitle>

@*
    Public privacy policy for the SPIC ONE app. The Web host serves it at
    https://spicone.in/privacy, which is the URL registered with Google Play and the
    App Store; the mobile app shows the same page from its login footer.
    Review the wording with SPIC before the store listing goes live.
*@

<div class="pp-page">
    <header class="pp-header">
        <img src="_content/SPIC.MauiBlazorApp.Shared/Images/LoginImages/logo.png" alt="SPIC" class="pp-logo" />
        <div>
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="pp-sub">SPIC ONE mobile, desktop and web application &middot; Last updated 19 September 2026</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="pp-back" @onclick="GoBack">Back</button>
    </header>

    <main class="pp-content">
        <section>
            <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
            <p>
                SPIC ONE is the dealer, distributor and employee operations application of
                <strong>Southern Petrochemical Industries Corporation Limited (SPIC)</strong>,
                SPIC House, 88 Anna Salai, Little Mount, Guindy, Chennai 600032, India ("SPIC", "we").
                The application is developed and operated for SPIC by APM Technologies (apmiot.com).
                SPIC is the data controller for the personal data described here.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>2. Who can use the app</h2>
            <p>
                SPIC ONE is not a public consumer app. Accounts are created by SPIC for its dealers,
                sub-dealers, distributors, retailers, employees and authorised partners. There is no
                self sign-up.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>3. Data we collect</h2>
            <table class="pp-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Why</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Account and contact details</td>
                        <td>Name, user name, designation, mobile number, email, dealer code</td>
                        <td>Sign-in, role-based access, communication about your registrations and applications</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Business registration data</td>
                        <td>Firm name, address, GST number, PAN, bank account details, turnover, warehouse and market details</td>
                        <td>Dealer and sub-dealer registration, credit-limit assessment, statutory compliance</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Identity and supporting documents</td>
                        <td>Aadhaar, PAN card, GST certificate, cancelled cheque, income-tax returns, property and licence documents uploaded by you</td>
                        <td>Verification of the dealer or applicant as required by SPIC's dealership and welfare-scheme processes</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Welfare and guest-house applications</td>
                        <td>Family member details, education records, booking dates, guest ID proof, payment references</td>
                        <td>Processing the scheme or booking you applied for</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Location</td>
                        <td>GPS coordinates captured only when you press a "use my location" control</td>
                        <td>Recording dealer, warehouse, rake point and logistics positions on a map</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Photos and files</td>
                        <td>Images and documents you choose from your device</td>
                        <td>Attachments to registrations, applications and reports</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Technical data</td>
                        <td>App version, device platform, IP address, sign-in time, server logs</td>
                        <td>Security, troubleshooting, keeping the service running</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p>
                The app does not read your contacts, messages, call logs or browsing history, does not
                run location tracking in the background, and does not show advertising.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>4. How we use the data</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>To operate the dealer network: registrations, approvals, credit limits, stock and sales reporting.</li>
                <li>To process SPIC welfare schemes, lucky draws and guest-house bookings you apply for.</li>
                <li>To meet legal and statutory obligations, including GST and fertiliser-sector reporting.</li>
                <li>To secure the service, prevent misuse and keep audit trails of approvals.</li>
                <li>To contact you about the status of your requests, by phone, SMS, WhatsApp or email.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do not sell personal data and we do not use it for third-party advertising or profiling.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
            <p>Personal data is shared only with:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>SPIC staff and approving officers whose role requires it (state, regional and head-office teams).</li>
                <li>APM Technologies, as the processor that develops and hosts the application on SPIC's behalf.</li>
                <li>Cloud hosting providers used to run the service (Microsoft Azure, India region). Data stays within India unless a regulator requires otherwise.</li>
                <li>Government portals and authorities where a law or a subsidy scheme requires reporting.</li>
                <li>Map tiles are loaded from OpenStreetMap when you open a map; only the map area requested is sent to that service.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>6. Retention</h2>
            <p>
                Registration and approval records are kept for the life of the dealership relationship and for
                the period required by Indian company, tax and fertiliser regulations thereafter (normally eight
                years). Welfare-scheme and booking records are kept for the scheme's audit period. Uploaded
                documents that are rejected or withdrawn are deleted within 90 days of the decision. Technical
                logs are kept for 30 days.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>7. Security</h2>
            <p>
                Data is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). Your sign-in token is stored in the device's secure store
                (Android Keystore, iOS Keychain, Windows credential protection) and expires automatically.
                Access inside SPIC is limited by role and logged. Uploaded documents are held on access-controlled
                cloud storage, not on the device.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
            <p>
                Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 you may ask for access to, correction of, or
                erasure of your personal data, and you may withdraw consent for optional processing such as
                location. Erasure requests are honoured except where SPIC must keep the record by law. To exercise
                these rights, or to close your account, contact the SPIC ONE support desk below. We reply within
                30 days.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>9. Children</h2>
            <p>The app is for business users aged 18 and over and is not directed at children.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>
                We will post any change on this page and update the date above. Material changes will also be
                announced inside the app.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>11. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                SPIC ONE Support, Southern Petrochemical Industries Corporation Limited,<br />
                SPIC House, 88 Anna Salai, Little Mount, Guindy, Chennai 600032, India.<br />
                Email: <a href="mailto:sdwa@spic.co.in">sdwa@spic.co.in</a>
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="pp-footer">&copy; @DateTime.Now.Year SPIC ONE</footer>
</div>

@code {
    private void GoBack() => Nav.NavigateTo("/login");
}
